Source: homelab-mailsend
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab-api

Package: homelab-mailsend
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, postfix, postfix-pgsql, postgresql-client,
 opendmarc, opendkim, adduser
Description: Postfix provisioning for Homelab mail (virtual domains, SASL, DKIM/DMARC)
 Wires Postfix's PostgreSQL-backed virtual domain/alias/recipient-access/
 sender-login-maps lookups, SASL delegation to Dovecot, and DKIM/DMARC
 milter integration -- via postconf -e (idempotent, additive-only) and a
 pre-checked, sentinel-guarded master.cf block that refuses to insert
 over an already-existing hand-written submission/smtps listener.
 Integrates with whichever DKIM signer is actually live (OpenDKIM by
 default, matching production) rather than reimplementing DKIM signing.
